# Environment variables for the contact form (EmailJS).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the project root — the same directory as
# `package.json` — and fill in the three values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed. Vite only reads `.env`
# files from the project root, and only exposes variables prefixed with
# `VITE_` to client code, so all three names below are required verbatim.
# Restart `npm run dev` after editing `.env`; Vite reads it at startup.
#
# The values come from the EmailJS dashboard at https://dashboard.emailjs.com:
#
#   SERVICE_ID   Email Services  -> the service you connected
#   TEMPLATE_ID  Email Templates -> the template the form sends
#   PUBLIC_KEY   Account -> General -> Public Key
#
# These are public by design: the bundle ships them to the browser. Keep the
# EmailJS private key out of this project, and set the allowed origins in the
# EmailJS dashboard so the service cannot be called from anywhere else.
#
# For the deployed site the same three variables are set in the Netlify
# dashboard under Site configuration -> Environment variables, not in a file.

VITE_APP_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_APP_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_APP_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
